1
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,060
<i>They've adapted to each other's weapons,</i>

2
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,020
<i>bringing out their abilities,</i>

3
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,850
<i>and developed a three-man combination</i>

4
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:26,020
<i>that surpasses geniuses like Barou and Nagi!</i>

5
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:32,530
<i>They're incredibly strong.</i>

6
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:36,240
<i>A team that balances offense and defense perfectly,</i>

7
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,670
<i>with no openings.</i>

8
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:40,700
<i>Even so, I can't help but want</i>

9
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,940
<i>to test myself against them.</i>

10
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:47,960
<i>Our new, stronger team, and this team's chemical reaction.</i>

11
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:49,500
Let's go.

12
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,760
I was born ready.

13
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:53,800
Don't order me around.

14
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:34,780
<i>Blind spot and off the ball area.</i>

15
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:39,910
<i>I'll combine these new pieces with my spatial awareness.</i>

16
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:43,910
<i>This is my new field vision.</i>

17
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:45,620
<i>Perceive the vision of everyone,</i>

18
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,580
<i>friend and foe alike.</i>

19
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:53,590
<i>Now, I can see each player's movements much more clearly than before.</i>

20
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:58,670
<i>The paths to the goal are flooding into my brain!</i>

21
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,720
Barou!

22
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,220
<i>Come on, Reo, right there.</i>

23
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:08,850
<i>When he makes his move to turn towards me, I'll go the opposite way!</i>

24
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:12,650
<i>I passed him! The path to the goal is open.</i>

25
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:14,650
<i>Now. Pass, Barou!</i>

26
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:18,280
<i>Is this for real?</i>

27
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:21,240
Even for our selfish king,

28
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:22,700
<i>this is too much!</i>

29
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,790
Come on. I'll handle Chigiri somehow.

30
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,710
Don't let Reo get the ball!

31
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,500
I know, but...

32
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:34,000
<i>No way.</i>

33
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,550
<i>If we leave Kunigami free at mid-range,</i>

34
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:39,130
<i>he'll shoot.</i>

35
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:42,760
Go on.

36
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,720
Take this!

37
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,020
Nice shot, Kunigami!

38
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:51,440
Damn, they're really good.

39
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:53,690
Barou.

40
00:03:53,770 --> 00:03:55,150
Cut it out already.

41
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,940
Isagi was completely open.

42
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,690
Why didn't you pass?

43
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,200
Shut up.

44
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:05,160
Who passes just so someone else can score?

45
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:07,580
Are you stupid?

46
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:09,660
What's the point if we can't win?

47
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,710
Yeah, with my goal.

48
00:04:11,790 --> 00:04:14,960
You two should be playing to make me comfortable.

49
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,000
Enough!

50
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:18,460
I'll make the passes for now.

51
00:04:18,550 --> 00:04:19,670
Then I'm next.

52
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,630
No, me.

53
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,050
<i>These two can't get along.</i>

54
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:28,430
<i>I have to control this team.</i>

55
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:37,190
<i>I have to reunite them.</i>

56
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:44,110
<i>I have to find a way to create a chemical reaction with the three of us, with Nagi and Barou.</i>

57
00:04:47,990 --> 00:04:50,620
<i>I need to refresh my field vision.</i>

58
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:52,040
<i>I have to lead this team</i>

59
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:55,540
<i>to the goal!</i>

60
00:05:00,210 --> 00:05:01,260
<i>Seriously?</i>

61
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,720
<i>Even if I pass to Barou,</i>

62
00:05:04,590 --> 00:05:06,090
<i>it's completely dead after that.</i>

63
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:11,810
<i>In my current state, I can't create a chemical reaction with Barou.</i>

64
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:14,890
<i>What about Nagi?</i>

65
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:20,320
<i>He has infinite goal routes!</i>

66
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:26,530
<i>Nagi is moving according to my pass.</i>

67
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:30,410
<i>I've developed enough to notice</i>

68
00:05:30,490 --> 00:05:32,200
<i>his off-the-ball movements.</i>

69
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:33,580
<i>Go, Nagi.</i>

70
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:34,620
<i>Here, right?</i>

71
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:38,080
A fast pass. Are you challenging me?

72
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:41,420
You know what? No matter how fast you are,

73
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,300
people can't suddenly

74
00:05:46,550 --> 00:05:48,390
turn the other way.

75
00:05:50,390 --> 00:05:51,430
<i>Amazing!</i>

76
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:55,140
<i>He dodged Chigiri, who came at full speed, by going the opposite way</i>

77
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,020
<i>and created a path to the goal.</i>

78
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,770
<i>A play beyond even my vision.</i>

79
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,320
<i>This is</i>

80
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:06,490
<i>our chemical reaction!</i>

81
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:08,160
ISAGI YOICHI X NAGI SEISHIRO

82
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,910
We're one step closer.

83
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:15,080
Is he a monster?

84
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,370
Seriously?

85
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:19,330
This guy's better than last time.

86
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,090
Nice pass, Isagi.

87
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:28,010
From now on, let's advance and win together.

88
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:28,930
Okay.

89
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,510
<i>No.</i>

90
00:06:30,590 --> 00:06:32,890
<i>We're just barely holding on this way.</i>

91
00:06:32,970 --> 00:06:35,720
<i>Triggering a chemical reaction with Barou is all that's left.</i>

92
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:38,560
<i>I'm sure that's the key to victory!</i>

93
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:43,110
Look, Barou. Please listen.

94
00:06:44,650 --> 00:06:45,980
Right now,

95
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:48,780
I can't smell a goal from you.

96
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,370
Play in a way that lets Nagi and me score.

97
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:54,540
That's the only way we can keep up with each other.

98
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:57,960
I can't trigger a chemical reaction alone.

99
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:01,080
How many times do I have to tell you, loser?

100
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:04,420
I will win with my own goal.

101
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:08,300
I'd rather die than play for someone else.

102
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,260
But

103
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:14,010
if you pass to me, it could create more opportunities.

104
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,970
Those opportunities could also result in your goal.

105
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,520
Opportunities aren't enough.

106
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:24,110
I win the way I want to win. I refuse everything else.

107
00:07:24,190 --> 00:07:27,190
I'm telling you, we're going to lose this way.

108
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,690
No problem at all.

109
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:32,780
I'd rather lose than give up my rules and win.

110
00:07:33,570 --> 00:07:38,450
Why can't you see that you're ruining your own potential with this mindset?

111
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:43,130
You're more than this.

112
00:07:43,210 --> 00:07:47,340
I teamed up with you because I thought we could get even stronger!

113
00:07:48,090 --> 00:07:49,130
At this rate,

114
00:07:49,210 --> 00:07:51,590
you're going to disappear right here.

115
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,090
Hey,

116
00:07:55,050 --> 00:07:57,390
watch your mouth, loser.

117
00:07:58,930 --> 00:08:02,350
Why can't I win despite having this talent?

118
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:06,020
Isn't it obvious that I'm the one

119
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:09,650
most frustrated with myself, you dumbass!

120
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,530
Who cares about a chemical reaction?

121
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:17,530
Who cares about playing together?

122
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:22,120
This is the soccer you want to play.

123
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,750
It makes me sick.

124
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,210
'Do as I say.'

125
00:08:29,250 --> 00:08:33,630
That's all I hear from you, loser.

126
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:40,390
In the end, we're both egoists.

127
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:44,060
We're creatures who can't do anything but what we want to do.

128
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:47,610
Don't think you can control me!

129
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:51,900
Don't waste your breath.

130
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:54,610
Even without Barou,

131
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:56,950
the two of us can win.

132
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,620
Yeah, you're right.

133
00:09:01,830 --> 00:09:05,670
<i>Damn it! Why am I so fixated on Barou?</i>

134
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,580
<i>Is it to win this match?</i>

135
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:11,510
<i>Or is it because Barou is wasting his potential?</i>

136
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:15,630
<i>How can I trigger a chemical reaction with Barou?</i>

137
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,640
Even so, that guy

138
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:23,480
can keep playing the king even when it's useless.

139
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:30,610
Unless you accept defeat, you can't understand true frustration.

140
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:38,820
Hey, Isagi Yoichi.

141
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:41,740
There's something I don't get.

142
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:46,210
Why did Nagi choose someone like you?

143
00:09:46,290 --> 00:09:47,750
<i>What's with this?</i>

144
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:49,670
<i>I'm tired of it.</i>

145
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:51,210
How would I know?

146
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:53,880
So, are you that talented then?

147
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:55,470
I

148
00:09:56,220 --> 00:10:00,220
don't have special weapons like you, Chigiri, or Kunigami.

149
00:10:00,930 --> 00:10:02,430
So in this match,

150
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:04,640
I'm only going to focus on winning!

151
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,140
<i>His maneuvering is great!</i>

152
00:10:07,230 --> 00:10:09,730
<i>Even without Chigiri's speed or Kunigami's physique,</i>

153
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:13,030
<i>I can't stop him with my average abilities.</i>

154
00:10:13,110 --> 00:10:18,610
<i>By winning this match, I'll make you regret choosing Yoichi Isagi.</i>

155
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,200
We're going, Reo.

156
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:22,240
You bastards.

157
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:25,080
<i>Damn it, they got past us.</i>

158
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:29,080
<i>The core of their team is, without a doubt, Reo!</i>

159
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:33,170
<i>A support player who balances defense and offense using Chigiri's weapon on the right</i>

160
00:10:33,250 --> 00:10:36,170
<i>and Kunigami's weapon on the left.</i>

161
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:40,890
<i>If Chigiri and Kunigami are players with one excessively developed talent,</i>

162
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:44,220
<i>Reo would be a player who is an expert in all skills.</i>

163
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:48,690
<i>His flawless all-around style is his true nature.</i>

164
00:10:48,770 --> 00:10:49,650
Chigiri!

165
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:52,020
You can't pass anymore.

166
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:54,270
Bring it on, redhead.

167
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:58,740
Come on, don't lump me in with your selfish king.

168
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,950
I'm not just about leaving you in the dust!

169
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,240
<i>Did he send it to the center?</i>

170
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:05,450
<i>I have to stop it!</i>

171
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,000
<i>I have to cut Reo off.</i>

172
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:07,950
Move!

173
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:16,630
That's it!

174
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,840
<i>A perfectly balanced three-man combination.</i>

175
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:24,430
<i>These guys are insanely strong!</i>

176
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,890
<i>Maybe I should stop obsessing over Barou?</i>

177
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:35,400
<i>Maybe it's time to think about winning with just Nagi.</i>

178
00:11:36,150 --> 00:11:39,400
<i>No, it's impossible. I can't visualize us winning with just Nagi.</i>

179
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:42,030
<i>We'd score one or two goals and then be finished.</i>

180
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:44,450
<i>Think!</i>

181
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:51,000
<i>You are an adaptable genius!</i>

182
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:55,540
<i>Does adapting mean getting stronger based on the opponent like this?</i>

183
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,470
<i>I see.</i>

184
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:02,760
<i>I won't move him.</i>

185
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:09,770
<i>I'll devour Barou!</i>

186
00:12:18,230 --> 00:12:20,240
<i>I was mistaken.</i>

187
00:12:21,110 --> 00:12:24,990
<i>I thought I'd find the answer by adapting to Barou.</i>

188
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,950
<i>But this,</i>

189
00:12:27,030 --> 00:12:30,000
Don't think you can control me.

190
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:34,250
<i>This means hoping to control someone and change them.</i>

191
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,710
<i>That's not adaptation.</i>

192
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:42,010
<i>I don't play soccer to conform to others.</i>

193
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:44,050
<i>I'm here to win.</i>

194
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:48,560
Because you're not afraid to change.

195
00:12:49,350 --> 00:12:52,600
<i>Use your skills differently to win.</i>

196
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:57,860
<i>Don't depend on Barou. Instead of taking advantage of his play,</i>

197
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:03,570
<i>I'll devour his play and dominate the field!</i>

198
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:07,570
Nagi, we're going to win together.

199
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:10,540
Finally, you're on board.

200
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,750
Don't take your eyes off me.

201
00:13:12,830 --> 00:13:14,000
Yes, sir.

202
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:21,300
<i>The score is 1-3.</i>

203
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:23,510
<i>We have to score the next goal.</i>

204
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:27,340
<i>Looking at things so far,</i>

205
00:13:27,430 --> 00:13:29,100
<i>they're focused on Nagi's movements.</i>

206
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:33,850
<i>Reo is holding me so I can't pass to Nagi.</i>

207
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,190
<i>Even if I do pass,</i>

208
00:13:36,270 --> 00:13:39,650
<i>they're lined up to trap him instantly.</i>

209
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:43,070
<i>Kunigami's marking on Barou is noticeably weak.</i>

210
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:46,610
<i>But even with that, he knows he can hold Barou.</i>

211
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:51,080
<i>Barou can no longer be used in this match.</i>

212
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:55,040
<i>That's the current consensus on the field.</i>

213
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,040
<i>But in reality,</i>

214
00:13:56,120 --> 00:14:00,500
<i>the routes to Nagi have decreased compared to before.</i>

215
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:02,460
<i>Then I</i>

216
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,920
will choose Barou!

217
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,810
- He's dribbling instead of passing?
- Isagi?

218
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,800
The right decision, loser.

219
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,010
<i>Run, king.</i>

220
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:12,220
<i>Beg me for a pass!</i>

221
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:13,970
Shit! Like I'd let it go!

222
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,930
<i>That's right, Kunigami.</i>

223
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,600
<i>Get dragged along by Barou's attack.</i>

224
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:23,360
<i>After all, my target is the genius behind him.</i>

225
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,030
<i>Take this, Nagi!</i>

226
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:27,280
Seriously?

227
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,660
He caught up to us.

228
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,820
<i>This guy,</i>

229
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,830
<i>by pretending to pass to Barou and dribbling instead,</i>

230
00:14:32,910 --> 00:14:37,330
<i>drew their attention away from Nagi and created an opening to pass.</i>

231
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,790
Nice, Isagi.

232
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,170
I won't allow it!

233
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:43,960
Don't fall for it! Nagi will get past you with his control!

234
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:47,880
Damn it.

235
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:50,340
I thought I got past you.

236
00:14:50,430 --> 00:14:53,810
We barely scraped by. That was a sweet trap.

237
00:14:53,890 --> 00:14:55,390
Good job, princess!

238
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:56,770
Let's pressure and crush them!

239
00:14:56,850 --> 00:14:59,640
As long as you stop, you're useless.

240
00:14:59,730 --> 00:15:00,810
Pass to me!

241
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,650
Over here, asshole!

242
00:15:02,730 --> 00:15:03,610
Barou.

243
00:15:03,690 --> 00:15:06,400
I said I won't allow it, didn't I?

244
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:09,360
We'll handle Nagi!

245
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:13,740
<i>There.</i>

246
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:16,620
<i>Everyone is focused on me.</i>

247
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:19,370
<i>An area that no one else can see.</i>

248
00:15:20,710 --> 00:15:23,630
<i>You were waiting for the moment</i>

249
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:25,550
<i>to cut through the darkness!</i>

250
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:27,960
I never took my eyes off you.

251
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:29,720
- Huh?
- What?

252
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:33,140
<i>Seriously? Was everything from the start</i>

253
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:37,930
<i>for Isagi to score a goal?</i>

254
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:40,350
<i>This guy,</i>

255
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:42,310
<i>he devoured it!</i>

256
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:48,030
<i>No matter how much you touch someone's heart, people can't change others.</i>

257
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,910
<i>That's why you have to change yourself.</i>

258
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:55,660
<i>This is the only way to change a world</i>

259
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:58,580
<i>that doesn't go the way you want.</i>

260
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:01,210
<i>If I can't see a light leading to the goal,</i>

261
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:03,880
<i>then I'll become that light myself!</i>

262
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,380
<i>Look at me, Barou!</i>

263
00:16:07,050 --> 00:16:09,040
<i>I will adapt to you!</i>

264
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:12,050
<i>This darkness you create on the field,</i>

265
00:16:13,470 --> 00:16:14,760
<i>I'll devour it</i>

266
00:16:15,550 --> 00:16:17,100
<i>and turn it into light!</i>

267
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,390
Fuck!

268
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:25,480
<i>That bastard, for his own goal</i>

269
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,650
<i>he used me!</i>

270
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,490
Look at this guy.

271
00:16:33,570 --> 00:16:36,030
Did he see everything?

272
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,330
<i>This is Yoichi Isagi.</i>

273
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:43,670
<i>The egoist that Nagi Seishiro is following.</i>

274
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,630
Then let's turn this around.

275
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:49,090
Okay.

276
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,090
Also, Barou,

277
00:16:51,170 --> 00:16:53,800
you keep playing your usual game.

278
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,430
Don't get in the way.

279
00:16:57,220 --> 00:17:00,310
I said, don't get in my way,

280
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:01,350
loser.

281
00:17:05,350 --> 00:17:09,650
<i>Who do you think you're calling a loser?</i>

282
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,240
<i>I'll kill him.</i>

283
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:14,280
<i>I'll definitely prove it.</i>

284
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:18,370
<i>I am the king of this field!</i>

285
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:26,830
<i>There's clearly no trace of how he was just a moment ago.</i>

286
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:29,710
<i>What can he see?</i>

287
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:34,340
<i>As long as I don't understand, facing him is too risky.</i>

288
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:37,050
<i>Since they also know this,</i>

289
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:40,140
<i>they're focusing on Isagi and waiting for a pass.</i>

290
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:43,390
<i>In this case, I'm not the playmaker.</i>

291
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,390
Got it.

292
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:47,150
<i>The passing play we practiced.</i>

293
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:49,360
<i>Straight to Kunigami!</i>

294
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:50,690
Thanks.

295
00:17:51,190 --> 00:17:52,570
<i>If the pass doesn't come,</i>

296
00:17:52,650 --> 00:17:54,070
<i>I'll go and get it myself!</i>

297
00:17:54,150 --> 00:17:56,950
I didn't expect you to be this desperate, king.

298
00:17:57,030 --> 00:18:00,450
This is a physical battle and I'll be the one to win!

299
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:02,830
Just watch.

300
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:05,000
This ball is mine!

301
00:18:06,830 --> 00:18:08,500
Pass, Barou! Counter!

302
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:10,250
To hell with you! I've got it!

303
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:14,760
Why don't you ever listen to your people, king?

304
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,470
That's right!

305
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:18,760
<i>Did I lose again? Shit.</i>

306
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,800
<i>I'll go again and then…</i>

307
00:18:24,430 --> 00:18:27,390
<i>Wait, why was he standing there?</i>

308
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,900
<i>Could it be</i>

309
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:35,280
<i>that he went there knowing this would happen when Barou won the ball?</i>

310
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:39,110
<i>Isagi is developing incredibly fast.</i>

311
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:41,950
<i>I can't fall behind!</i>

312
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:46,700
<i>A pass? How can you be so calm?</i>

313
00:18:49,290 --> 00:18:50,540
Thanks.

314
00:18:57,130 --> 00:18:59,220
Nice. We caught them.

315
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:04,470
<i>Is he reading all our moves?</i>

316
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:07,180
<i>Right now, this field</i>

317
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:11,310
<i>is completely under their control!</i>

318
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,280
<i>We'll lose if we don't do something.</i>

319
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:20,570
<i>If we keep relying on our weapons, they'll beat us!</i>

320
00:19:21,450 --> 00:19:22,950
Run, Chigiri!

321
00:19:23,030 --> 00:19:27,250
<i>Just as Nagi said, my weakness is my ball control.</i>

322
00:19:27,330 --> 00:19:30,540
I know how to stop you, princess.

323
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,880
<i>No matter how fast I run,</i>

324
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,750
<i>I slow down when controlling the ball.</i>

325
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:40,300
<i>He aims to use this weakness of mine to stop me.</i>

326
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,340
<i>In that case…</i>

327
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,430
<i>all or nothing!</i>

328
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:45,310
<i>This control</i>

329
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:48,850
<i>will allow the ball to keep moving without stopping!</i>

330
00:19:49,890 --> 00:19:55,480
<i>It works! I can dribble at the same speed without cutting my high speed.</i>

331
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:57,690
<i>This is my 'non-stop' dribble!</i>

332
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,070
<i>Stop me if you can, Barou.</i>

333
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,870
<i>I'm not like you.</i>

334
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:10,040
<i>I'll drag you into my high-speed zone. This is my new technique!</i>

335
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:13,460
<i>You can't control</i>

336
00:20:14,170 --> 00:20:16,920
<i>me and my speed!</i>

337
00:20:27,310 --> 00:20:29,930
Did he just evolve?

338
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:32,310
This is insane.

339
00:20:34,190 --> 00:20:37,150
An egoist who hits rock bottom before us

340
00:20:38,110 --> 00:20:42,070
has no chance of becoming the world's best striker.

341
00:22:17,710 --> 00:22:20,420
<i>Blue Lock, Extra Time.</i>

342
00:22:21,130 --> 00:22:22,500
Damn it.

343
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:25,380
It took me ages to pass that stage.

344
00:22:25,470 --> 00:22:27,050
Who should I team up with?

345
00:22:27,130 --> 00:22:28,680
Raichi.

346
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:33,010
There's no one here. Looks like everyone's already gone.

347
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:36,100
Like Naruhaya. And also Naruhaya.

348
00:22:36,890 --> 00:22:39,350
I wouldn't have teamed up with him anyway, whatever.

349
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:41,690
So you're the only one left?

350
00:22:41,770 --> 00:22:45,650
I'd have liked to team up with Nagi or Isagi or something.

351
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,070
By the way...

352
00:22:47,780 --> 00:22:50,700
You're so annoying, Wanima bro!

353
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:52,870
What do you want, huh?!

354
00:22:52,950 --> 00:22:54,910
Ah, I see.

355
00:22:54,990 --> 00:22:57,710
Your brother used to translate for you.

356
00:22:57,790 --> 00:23:00,540
Come on, let's try to figure out what you want to say.

357
00:23:01,670 --> 00:23:03,800
Where can I buy sushi?

358
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:06,090
READ WANIMA'S FACIAL EXPRESSIONS WANIMA (BRO)!

359
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:09,340
Where can I find a samurai?

360
00:23:12,050 --> 00:23:14,560
Are you a tourist from overseas?

361
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:18,350
I don't care at all about that traitor.

362
00:23:18,430 --> 00:23:20,730
I'm sure he's complaining about something.

363
00:23:20,810 --> 00:23:23,190
That's not right!

364
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:26,980
Wait!

365
00:23:27,070 --> 00:23:29,070
<i>- He spoke normally! - He spoke normally!</i>

366
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:31,240
You two, listen to me.

367
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:33,160
Raichi Jingo!

368
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:36,240
First of all, I love how hard you are to knock down.

369
00:23:36,330 --> 00:23:38,830
That's not something a normal person can do.

370
00:23:38,910 --> 00:23:40,500
Despite your rough play style,

371
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:42,460
your soccer intelligence and tenacity stand out.

372
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:45,920
It's undeniable that you're the one who got us this far.

373
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,420
And Gagamaru Gin!

374
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:51,160
Your unexpected and original play style makes you one of a kind.

375
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,510
It seems like you're making random moves,

376
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:55,220
but in reality, you rely on your flexibility,

377
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:58,060
and by choosing the most suitable option,

378
00:23:58,140 --> 00:24:00,060
you've won me over.

379
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:03,480
So I thought I'd be compatible with you too

380
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:05,690
and teamed up with you.

381
00:24:05,770 --> 00:24:07,980
Wow. Is that what you think?

382
00:24:08,820 --> 00:24:09,990
Can't be helped.

383
00:24:10,070 --> 00:24:12,490
RAICHI, WANIMA, GAGAMARU FORMED A TEAM